1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:06,600
A campus timetable is a network of people, rooms, groups, events, and exams.

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:10,331
TESSRA turns that complexity into one governed workflow.

3
00:00:10,331 --> 00:00:16,499
The official Chilika Institute dataset contains twenty-seven rooms, forty faculty, fourteen groups, sixty-two courses,

4
00:00:16,499 --> 00:00:21,502
one hundred and eighty-nine sessions, twenty-five booking requests, and forty-one exams.

5
00:00:21,502 --> 00:00:26,080
This walkthrough combines the working product with concise technical evidence.

6
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:29,084
We begin in the real application.

7
00:00:29,084 --> 00:00:33,342
Role-based sign-in opens the correct workspace without exposing another role's actions.

8
00:00:33,342 --> 00:00:37,870
The Admin dashboard combines six live campus-health indicators, pending approvals, academic activity,

9
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:40,324
and fast links to common operations.

10
00:00:40,324 --> 00:00:45,574
In Smart Scheduling, the published timetable can be read by student group, faculty member,

11
00:00:45,574 --> 00:00:46,584
or room.

12
00:00:46,584 --> 00:00:50,120
Changing the view immediately queries the same validated schedule.

13
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:55,370
The venue finder then combines room type, capacity, features, date, time, maintenance, classes, exams,

14
00:00:55,370 --> 00:00:56,651
and approved events,

15
00:00:56,651 --> 00:01:02,352
so an apparently empty room is never offered when another campus commitment already occupies it.

16
00:01:02,902 --> 00:01:05,708
The Club workspace demonstrates an end-to-end booking.

17
00:01:05,708 --> 00:01:09,592
A representative describes the request in ordinary English or Hinglish.

18
00:01:09,592 --> 00:01:14,826
TESSRA extracts date, time, attendance, equipment, and the preferred venue into an editable draft;

19
00:01:14,826 --> 00:01:16,553
nothing is booked automatically.

20
00:01:16,553 --> 00:01:21,876
Priority remains code-controlled, so prompt text cannot impersonate a higher authority or bypass approval.

21
00:01:21,876 --> 00:01:27,110
On submission, the server checks timetable occupancy, exams, existing bookings, room fit, mandatory groups,

22
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:29,196
lead time, and role policy.

23
00:01:29,196 --> 00:01:32,271
The request then appears in the Admin queue,

24
00:01:32,271 --> 00:01:35,706
where approval is revalidated at the moment of decision

25
00:01:35,706 --> 00:01:38,512
and the requester receives a tracked outcome.

26
00:01:39,062 --> 00:01:43,567
The same operational model supports examinations, targeted notices, and disruptions.

27
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:48,489
Exam screens expose room capacity, groups, invigilation, and conflicts before publication.

28
00:01:48,489 --> 00:01:52,994
Notices can target a role or department and record acknowledgement.

29
00:01:52,994 --> 00:01:59,480
Campus Health stays intentionally compact, summarizing academic progress, faculty availability, room use, pending work, events,

30
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:01,065
and scheduling efficiency.

31
00:02:01,065 --> 00:02:03,797
For an absence or room outage,

32
00:02:03,797 --> 00:02:10,388
TESSRA presents a before-and-after plan and keeps the timetable unchanged until an Admin approves it.

33
00:02:10,938 --> 00:02:17,629
Behind these screens, organiser JSON is schema-checked, cross-referenced, hashed, and stored with an immutable run.

34
00:02:17,629 --> 00:02:21,250
A private Python service uses Google OR-Tools CP-SAT,

35
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:25,400
while the untouched organiser validator checks the export independently.

36
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:28,703
H one places every session exactly once.

37
00:02:28,703 --> 00:02:31,159
H two prevents faculty overlap.

38
00:02:31,159 --> 00:02:36,156
H three prevents student-group overlap while counting an elective basket once.

39
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:40,730
H four prevents room overlap across teaching, events, and exams.

40
00:02:40,730 --> 00:02:44,457
H five enforces capacity, with exam capacity halved.

41
00:02:44,457 --> 00:02:49,878
H six enforces room type, and H seven excludes every faculty-unavailable period.

42
00:02:50,428 --> 00:02:52,606
H eight excludes room unavailability.

43
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:58,072
H nine allows teaching only in P one through P nine, blocks lunch crossing,

44
00:02:58,072 --> 00:03:02,505
and starts three-hour labs only at P two or P six.

45
00:03:02,505 --> 00:03:04,309
H ten guarantees accessibility.

46
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:06,488
H eleven synchronizes elective baskets.

47
00:03:06,488 --> 00:03:09,042
H twelve caps faculty daily hours.

48
00:03:09,042 --> 00:03:14,132
H thirteen allocates approved bookings by official priority while checking classes, rooms, bookings,

49
00:03:14,132 --> 00:03:15,560
and mandatory groups.

50
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,739
H fourteen preserves fixed sessions.

51
00:03:17,739 --> 00:03:22,829
Only then are S one through S six optimized: faculty avoidance weight two,

52
00:03:22,829 --> 00:03:28,295
group gaps weight one, days above six hours weight three, repeated course weight three,

53
00:03:28,295 --> 00:03:33,104
rooms below forty percent use weight one, and P nine weight one.

54
00:03:33,654 --> 00:03:38,048
The Official Dataset workbench makes that evidence visible inside the product.

55
00:03:38,048 --> 00:03:43,094
The baseline report shows zero hard violations, soft penalty three, exam penalty zero,

56
00:03:43,094 --> 00:03:48,513
and a booking score of sixty-five point five out of seventy, with twenty-one approvals,

57
00:03:48,513 --> 00:03:51,790
two alternatives, two rejections, and zero priority inversions.

58
00:03:51,790 --> 00:03:54,695
For the supplied disruption, repair is lexicographic.

59
00:03:54,695 --> 00:03:58,717
Phase one proves the minimum number of moved baseline sessions.

60
00:03:58,717 --> 00:04:02,739
Phase two fixes that count and optimizes the soft goals.

61
00:04:02,739 --> 00:04:08,251
The live diff shows eight necessary moves: two time changes and six room-only changes.

62
00:04:08,251 --> 00:04:10,783
Export stays locked until separate approval.

63
00:04:11,333 --> 00:04:15,573
The executed result places all one hundred and eighty-nine sessions,

64
00:04:15,573 --> 00:04:20,314
covering two hundred and forty-three teaching hours, and all forty-one exams.

65
00:04:20,314 --> 00:04:25,458
Both baseline and repair have zero hard violations and soft penalty three.

66
00:04:25,458 --> 00:04:31,004
Thirty-three Python tests and sixty-four TypeScript tests protect the engine and product rules.

67
00:04:31,004 --> 00:04:36,047
TESSRA is therefore not only a timetable generator; it is a working,

68
00:04:36,047 --> 00:04:41,191
role-aware campus operating system whose important decisions are validated, explained, and auditable.
